This product includes software developed at KU-CVLAB.

  LocoTrack (https://github.com/cvlab-kaist/locotrack)
  Copyright 2024 KU-CVLAB
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

  The PyTorch implementation is redistributed unmodified under vendor/locotrack/,
  with its own LICENSE and PROVENANCE.txt retained. DBtracker's model
  (dbtrack/model/dbtrack_model.py) re-parents LocoTrack's own modules rather than
  reimplementing them, and the released LocoTrack checkpoints are the starting
  weights for every DBtracker checkpoint.

LocoTrack is itself derived from TAPIR / tapnet:

  TAPIR (https://github.com/google-deepmind/tapnet)
  Copyright 2023 DeepMind Technologies Limited
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

Training data preparation uses one file from Kubric:

  Kubric (https://github.com/google-research/kubric)
  Copyright 2026 The Kubric Authors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

  challenges/point_tracking/dataset.py -- the add_tracks function, vendored into
  pydeps/kubric/ at install time rather than pip-installing the full package.

Training data is MOVi-E (movi_e/256x256) from gs://kubric-public/tfds, published
by Google under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Cross-track attention (jefftrack/model/cross_track.py) and the occluded-position
loss weighting (jefftrack/losses.py) are independent implementations written from
the description in:

  Karaev et al., "CoTracker3: Simpler and Better Point Tracking by
  Pseudo-Labelling Real Videos", arXiv:2410.11831

The ideas are credited to that work. No code, weights or tensors in this
repository derive from any implementation of it.
